# DSMLP job configuration for the E-STEER proof-of-concept.
#
# Copy this file to dsmlp.env (NOT tracked by git -- see ../../.gitignore)
# and fill in the values marked "FILL IN". Everything else is a reasonable
# default sized for this project (a 0.5B model, ~60 short generations) and
# can be left as-is or adjusted.
#
# Source: https://dsmlp-docs.ucsd.edu/ (launch.sh reference, job modes &
# limits, GPU classes, workspaces & storage). See README.md in this folder
# for the full explanation and citations for every value below.

# --- FILL IN: account- and workspace-specific values ---------------------

# Your DSMLP / UCSD AD username (used to ssh to the login node).
DSMLP_USERNAME=FILL_IN_YOUR_USERNAME

# Absolute path to this project AS SEEN INSIDE THE JOB CONTAINER (not the
# login node). If you rsync the folder to `~` on dsmlp-login, it appears in
# the container as /home/<username>/private/E-steer_2026 -- a plain `~` on
# the login node is mounted as private/ in containers. For a workspace home
# instead, use the path form shown by `workspace -l` on the login node.
# Docs: https://dsmlp-docs.ucsd.edu/workspaces-and-storage/moving-and-sharing-data/
PROJECT_DIR_ON_DSMLP=FILL_IN_/home/FILL_IN_YOUR_USERNAME/private/E-steer_2026

# --- Defaults you can adjust but don't have to -----------------------------

# GPU class: extra-small (~6GB), small (~12GB, RTX 2080Ti), medium (~24GB),
# large (~48GB), extra-large (~96GB). "small" comfortably fits this 0.5B
# model; raise it only if you intentionally scale the model up.
# Docs: https://dsmlp-docs.ucsd.edu/gpu-access/gpu-classes/
GPU_CLASS=small

# CPU cores / RAM (GB) / GPU count for the job.
CPUS=4
MEM_GB=16
GPUS=1

# Where steer.py/report.py write results.json, the plots, and SUMMARY.md on
# DSMLP. Defaults to a `results/` subfolder under the project so it never
# collides with (or overwrites) the local-run results already committed at
# the top of this folder. This path is git-ignored.
OUT_DIR=${PROJECT_DIR_ON_DSMLP}/results

# Where the per-user Python venv (transformers/numpy/matplotlib on top of
# the container's own PyTorch) is created. Lives in the home directory so it
# persists across jobs, per DSMLP's package-install guidance.
# Docs: https://dsmlp-docs.ucsd.edu/environments/customizing-your-environment/
VENV_DIR=${HOME}/.venvs/e-steer

# Where Hugging Face caches the downloaded model weights. Also in the home
# directory so the download only has to happen once.
HF_HOME_DIR=${HOME}/.cache/huggingface

# =====================================================================
# Paper-faithful job (faithful/): Qwen3-8B + SAE steering. Used only by
# submit_faithful.sh; the proof-of-concept scripts above ignore these.
# Full explanation and the budget/storage requirements: faithful/README.md
# =====================================================================

# Model tier. `auto` checks the GPU the job actually receives and picks the paper's Qwen3-8B if it fits (~21 GB:
# GPU class medium or larger), otherwise the smaller Qwen3-1.7B fallback (fits ~12 GB: class small). Force one with
# `qwen3-8b` or `qwen3-1.7b`. The 1.7B tier is NOT the paper's model (see faithful/README.md); it needs the
# `smaller-model` acknowledgement below.
FAITHFUL_MODEL_TIER=auto

# GPU class to request. medium (~24 GB: A30, A5000, or a slice of H100/RTX 6000) lets `auto` choose Qwen3-8B;
# large (~48 GB, 2 SU/GPU-hour vs 1) gives headroom; small (~12 GB) runs only the 1.7B tier; extra-small (~6 GB)
# is too small for either. Your workspace must have been granted the class -- confirm with datahub@ucsd.edu if a
# job stays Pending.
# Docs: https://dsmlp-docs.ucsd.edu/gpu-access/gpu-classes/  and  .../gpu-access/quotas-and-availability/
FAITHFUL_GPU_CLASS=medium
FAITHFUL_CPUS=8
FAITHFUL_MEM_GB=32

# Maximum job runtime in hours. DSMLP's default is 6 h and the documented maximum settable at launch is 12 h
# (longer needs a request to datahub@ucsd.edu). Runs are resumable: resubmit with the same RUN_ID.
# Docs: https://dsmlp-docs.ucsd.edu/running-jobs/job-modes-and-limits/
FAITHFUL_RUNTIME_HOURS=12

# Profile: smoke (plumbing only, tiny model -- not for DSMLP), pilot (real model, small samples, ~13 conditions),
# or full (all 19 conditions, default sample sizes). Start with pilot.
FAITHFUL_PROFILE=pilot

# Stages to run (comma-separated). agent is the most expensive stage; run it last, separately.
#   preflight,features,calibrate,llm,validation,agent,report
FAITHFUL_STAGES=preflight,features,calibrate,llm,validation,report

# Leave empty to start a new run (id = <profile>-<timestamp>). Set to an existing id to RESUME that run.
FAITHFUL_RUN_ID=

# FILL IN deliberately: the substitutions you accept for this run (see faithful/README.md "Fidelity matrix").
# The job refuses to start if a required one is missing. For the default stages above you need:
#   sae-qwen-scope,judge-backbone,alpha,subset-sizes     (+ label-handpicked if no NRC lexicon below)
#   (+ smaller-model if the run may use / falls back to the Qwen3-1.7B tier; harmless if the 8B tier is chosen)
#   (+ agent-reconstruction when the agent stage is included; + gaia-no-tools if gaia is enabled)
FAITHFUL_ACK=

# Optional: path (inside the container) to the NRC VAD Lexicon v2 text file. Download it yourself from
# https://saifmohammad.com/WebPages/nrc-vad.html (research use; it is not redistributed in this repo), rsync it to
# DSMLP, and put the container path here. Without it the hand-picked fallback is used (needs ack label-handpicked).
FAITHFUL_NRC_VAD_PATH=

# Outputs and logs, kept separate from the proof-of-concept's ${OUT_DIR}:
#   ${FAITHFUL_OUT_DIR}/<run_id>/   results, figures, REPORT.md, run.log
#   ~/e-steer-faithful-<run_id>.log  container stdout/stderr (home directory, so it survives pod deletion)
FAITHFUL_OUT_DIR=${PROJECT_DIR_ON_DSMLP}/results_faithful

# Separate venv from the proof-of-concept's so their pinned packages never conflict.
FAITHFUL_VENV_DIR=${HOME}/.venvs/e-steer-faithful

# Hugging Face cache: Qwen3-8B (~16.4 GB) + SAE (~2.1 GB) = ~20 GB, or Qwen3-1.7B (~4 GB) + SAE (~0.5 GB) = ~6 GB. DSMLP course homes
# are typically 5-10 GB and research workspaces ~100 GB (docs: workspaces-and-storage/your-files-and-quotas), so a
# course workspace may not be able to hold it -- check your quota before the first run (faithful/README.md).
FAITHFUL_HF_HOME_DIR=${HOME}/.cache/huggingface

# Project folder on the login node, RELATIVE to your login-node home directory (where rsync put it; this is not the
# container path above). Used only by fetch_faithful_results.sh, which you run on your laptop.
LOGIN_NODE_PROJECT_DIR=E-steer_2026
